 *2*::
 system does not provide the necessary functionality
 
+== NOTES
+
+A seccomp filter can change the result of any system call, including the ones programs use to check the *exec_restrict_file* and *exec_deny_interactive* securebits (see *setpriv*(1)). Since the filter built by *enosys* comes from its command line rather than from a file, *enosys* refuses to run _command_ when the *exec_deny_interactive* securebit is set. *--dump* still works: an administrator can save the filter to a file, give it execute permission, and load it with *setpriv --seccomp-filter*.
+
